  "id": "DrugBank_DB00747 - MONDO_grouped_11786_5324_24332",
  "verbalization": "Scopolamine is implicated in the pathogenesis of Allergic Rhinitis through a series of indirect pathways, all of which involve Vasomotor Rhinitis. The evidence suggests that Scopolamine acts as an indication for Vasomotor Rhinitis, which in turn is linked to two other drugs—Mizolastine and Ramatroban—that also indicate Allergic Rhinitis. This implies a shared mechanism of action or pathophysiological role in the development of allergic rhinitis. The presence of multiple drugs with similar indications for Vasomotor Rhinitis suggests that Scopolamine may exert a modulatory effect on the same biological processes that underlie Vasomotor Rhinitis, potentially through central or peripheral nervous system pathways. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of Vasomotor Rhinitis as a common intermediate in the relationship between Scopolamine and Allergic Rhinitis, reinforcing the notion of a broader pharmacological or pathophysiological link.",
